# Tests required with behaviour changes

## When this applies

Whenever you **add or materially change** code under **`domain/`**, **`application/`**, **`infrastructure/`**, **`server/`**, or **`shared/`** (logic, contracts, or HTTP handlers), **add or extend automated tests in the same task** unless the user explicitly scopes work as “no tests” or “docs/config only.”

## If no test exists yet

- **Create** a new test file rather than leaving behaviour uncovered.
- **Use-case classes**: `tests/unit/<bounded-context>/<name>.use-case.test.ts` (e.g. `tests/unit/competitions/…`) with **fakes** that implement the relevant **port interfaces**.
- **Nitro handlers**: prefer tests that exercise the handler or the use case it calls; use **`tests/nuxt/**`** only when the **Nuxt** runtime is required (e.g. components, composables).
- **Domain** (pure rules): colocate under `tests/unit/<context>/` or next to source—**no** separate `tests/domain/…` mirror is required.

## Before finishing

- Switch to **Node 22** (`.nvmrc`) if needed, then run **`npm run test -- --run`** (or **`npm run test:coverage`** when coverage is relevant) and fix **our** test failures.
- If Vitest fails to load with **`oxc-walker` / `parseSync`**, do **not** debug Nuxt or install oxc packages—see `.cursor/rules/vitest-oxc-trap.mdc`. Retry once on Node 22; otherwise skip and say why.
- If you skip tests, **say why** in the summary (e.g. spike only, blocked dependency).
